# --- Line endings -----------------------------------------------------------
# Target runtime is Linux/Bash + CUDA; this tree arrived CRLF from a Windows
# checkout, which is not harmless here: a trailing CR silently contaminates shell
# variables and paths (`x=1\r` != `1`, so comparisons and `cd` misbehave), and on
# Linux a CRLF shebang is not executable (`bad interpreter: ... bash\r`).
# `bash -n` catches neither. Store LF in the repository and check LF out
# everywhere, so a Windows working copy cannot reintroduce CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Frozen reference layer: the bytes themselves are the record ------------
# results/reference/** is a byte-for-byte copy (copy2) from the source tree, and 25
# of its manifests record source_sha256 / source_size_bytes of those raw bytes, CRLF
# included (e.g. nfe_scaling/line_tracing/vanilla_summary.json, 42181 bytes). Any
# normalization would invalidate those hashes, so this subtree is never converted.
# Seven files are the exception: on 2026-10-02 the cluster account paths inside
# their provenance strings were replaced with <CLUSTER_ROOT> (and, in cer_curves.json,
# the W&B account name with <WANDB_ENTITY>), which changes those bytes and only those
# bytes — reversing the substitutions reproduces the recorded source_sha256. Their
# manifests carry path_redaction / copy_sha256 / copy_size_bytes.
# See results/reference/README.md.
results/reference/** -text

# --- Binary payloads: never touch line endings or diffs ---------------------
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ttf binary
*.safetensors binary
*.bin binary
*.pt binary
*.pth binary
*.ckpt binary